WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:07.480
Cool, so we're making some good progress.

00:00:07.481 --> 00:00:12.240
We've added the rigid body to the player
so we can use forces, swing press play, our

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:17.240
player flies all the way into the air
and then drops all the way back down.

00:00:17.241 --> 00:00:19.354
Now we're gonna make
it so we can use input

00:00:19.366 --> 00:00:21.640
from the player to
actually control this jump.

00:00:21.641 --> 00:00:24.406
So if we go back into
our player controller

00:00:24.418 --> 00:00:27.520
script, we're going to go
into our update method

00:00:27.521 --> 00:00:33.840
and we're going to use an if statement and
in that if statement we're going to check

00:00:43.599 --> 00:00:45.325
whenever the player
presses the space bars

00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:47.200
and then inside of our
if statement, now what

00:00:47.201 --> 00:00:54.400
we're actually going to do is we're just
going to take our add force, cut it out of

00:00:54.549 --> 00:00:56.597
start so that way
the player doesn't just

00:00:56.609 --> 00:01:00.800
jump when it starts, although we
could do that because that'd be fun.

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:02.860
And in our if statement
we'll make it so that

00:01:02.872 --> 00:01:04.760
the player jumps
whenever we press space.

00:01:04.761 --> 00:01:07.780
Now one slight change
that we can make to

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:11.120
this to make it a lot
more immediate when the

00:01:11.121 --> 00:01:17.200
player jumps is by actually changing
our add force method just a little bit.

00:01:17.201 --> 00:01:23.280
So we're going to drop this back
down to 100, we'll say maybe 10 for now.

00:01:23.281 --> 00:01:27.560
So you can see when we were originally passing
in this parameter, we were just passing

00:01:27.561 --> 00:01:30.472
in a vector three, but you
can see when we added

00:01:30.473 --> 00:01:36.360
this comma that we can
actually add in a force mode.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:41.440
And so we can actually apply
different forces through this force mode.

00:01:41.441 --> 00:01:44.260
So in fact, if we actually
type in, oh, it auto

00:01:44.261 --> 00:01:47.720
completes force mode
for us, which is pretty nice.

00:01:47.721 --> 00:01:51.920
So we'll just type force mode.

00:01:51.921 --> 00:01:58.120
And then we're actually
going to apply an impulse force.

00:01:58.121 --> 00:02:01.720
Now there's four different kinds
of forces that you can apply.

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:07.320
There's a normal force force mode,
which applies that force over time.

00:02:07.321 --> 00:02:12.400
And this case force mode impulse immediately
applies the force that we want to apply.

00:02:12.401 --> 00:02:17.520
So in this case, you should see that
player jump happen a little bit faster.

00:02:17.521 --> 00:02:21.222
So if we go back
into unity, if we go to

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:29.440
our player and we focus on
them, and then we play our game.

00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:34.760
Now when we press space, you can see
that the player jumps almost immediately.

00:02:34.761 --> 00:02:36.979
And we in fact actually
need less force because

00:02:36.991 --> 00:02:39.080
we're not trying to
apply a force over time.

00:02:39.081 --> 00:02:41.080
We're just applying that force right now.

00:02:41.081 --> 00:02:43.680
So immediately they get to 10.

00:02:43.681 --> 00:02:46.068
So what you're going to
do is you're going to add

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:51.120
in your own if statement
to get the space bar input.

00:02:51.121 --> 00:02:53.699
And then you're going
to move that add force

00:02:53.711 --> 00:02:58.800
method from start down into our
update method inside the if statement.

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:00.930
And you're going to
change the parameters

00:03:00.942 --> 00:03:06.840
that you're putting in so that
it's a vector 3 up times 10.

00:03:06.841 --> 00:03:10.040
And you're applying the
force mode as an impulse.

00:03:10.041 --> 00:03:11.041
Now it's your turn.